{%- comment -%}
  The [#18022] token in a subject line, which is the cascade's fallback
  when a client drops the threading headers.

  Clients prefix a reply in their own language and their own case, and
  some of them do it twice. Every shape below arrives in real mail, and
  the token has to survive all of them or a reply opens a second ticket
  for a conversation that already exists.

  The rejections matter as much as the matches. Anything that is not a
  plain number between the brackets has to come back empty rather than
  as a half read number, because the value is used to look up a ticket
  and the wrong ticket is worse than none.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign cases = '[#18022],Re: a thing [#18022],RE: a thing [#18022],Re: RE: Fwd: a thing [#18022],AW: a thing [#18022],Antwort: a thing [#18022],R: a thing [#18022],a thing [#18022] trailing words' | split: ','
  for subject in cases
    function number = 'modules/support/helpers/email/ticket_number_from_subject', subject: subject
    assign label = 'finds the number in: ' | append: subject
    function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: number, expected: 18022, field_name: label
  endfor

  comment
    Two tokens. The last one wins, which is the one our own reply put
    there: a customer forwarding an old thread into a new one carries the
    older token further up the subject.
  endcomment
  function two = 'modules/support/helpers/email/ticket_number_from_subject', subject: 'Re: Fwd: old thing [#17001] new thing [#18022]'
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: two, expected: 18022, field_name: 'two tokens, the last one wins'

  comment
    Not a number, no token, or nothing between the brackets. All of these
    must be nothing rather than a guess.
  endcomment
  assign rejected = 'a thing with no token,[#],[# ],[#abc],[#18022x],[#18-022],[#1.5],Re: [#] a thing' | split: ','
  for subject in rejected
    function number = 'modules/support/helpers/email/ticket_number_from_subject', subject: subject
    assign label = 'refuses: ' | append: subject
    function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: number, expected: null, field_name: label
  endfor

  function no_subject = 'modules/support/helpers/email/ticket_number_from_subject', subject: null
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: no_subject, expected: null, field_name: 'no subject at all'

  comment
    A number is only ever honoured for someone already on that ticket,
    which is checked elsewhere. This helper's job is to read it, and it
    reads a large one as readily as a small one.
  endcomment
  function large = 'modules/support/helpers/email/ticket_number_from_subject', subject: 'Re: a thing [#1048576]'
  function contract = 'modules/tests/assertions/equal', contract: contract, given: large, expected: 1048576, field_name: 'a six figure number'
%}
